---
// "How to use ULC?" homepage section: one intro paragraph + two audience
// cards (designers, manufacturers). Copy sourced from the upstream README's
// "Who uses ULC" framing.
---

<section class="relative">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-20 md:px-10 md:py-28 lg:py-32">
    <h2
      class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-tight max-w-2xl"
    >
      How to use ULC?
    </h2>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-base md:text-lg text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
      ULC is consumed indirectly through tools that read it. AI agents, design
      software, specification tools, and data pipelines parse ULC files
      directly, without preprocessing PDFs, which saves time and money by
      reducing AI token consumption. Any JSON-aware system can consume the
      format, including general-purpose LLMs such as ChatGPT and Claude, and
      domain-specific AI tools such as
      {' '}<a
        href="https://www.lightingagent.ai/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-[var(--accent-warm)] hover:text-[var(--accent-warm-deep)] transition-colors underline underline-offset-4"
      >LightingAgent.AI</a>
      {' '}and{' '}
      <a
        href="https://www.gosourcery.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="text-[var(--accent-warm)] hover:text-[var(--accent-warm-deep)] transition-colors underline underline-offset-4"
      >gosourcery.com</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-10">
      <article
        class="border border-token rounded-lg p-8 md:p-10"
        style="background: var(--bg-elevated);"
      >
        <h3 class="small-caps text-xs text-[var(--text-subtle)]">
          For lighting designers
        </h3>
        <p
          class="mt-3 text-base md:text-lg text-[var(--text)] leading-relaxed"
        >
          Consume ULC data through tools that read it. Get fast, accurate,
          AI-assisted comparisons, luminaire schedules, and value engineering
          review.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/for-designers"
          class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--accent-warm)] hover:underline underline-offset-4"
        >
          Designer track <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </article>

      <article
        class="border border-token rounded-lg p-8 md:p-10"
        style="background: var(--bg-elevated);"
      >
        <h3 class="small-caps text-xs text-[var(--text-subtle)]">
          For lighting manufacturers
        </h3>
        <p
          class="mt-3 text-base md:text-lg text-[var(--text)] leading-relaxed"
        >
          Publish ULC files alongside your datasheet PDFs, IES, and LDT files
          on your product pages. Gain machine-discoverability by AI systems
          and improved data fidelity in downstream workflows.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/for-manufacturers"
          class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--accent-warm)] hover:underline underline-offset-4"
        >
          Manufacturer track <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
